window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-081fb98842811f87"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"turn-meetings-into-follow-ups\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">将会议转化为后续行动</h1> <p>把 Zoom 会议中的信息整理成各个工具中的后续事项。</p> <p>使用 ChatGPT 配合 Zoom 会议转录文本和 AI Companion 总结，起草客户跟进邮件、客户账户计划、CRM 更新和团队通知，供你审核。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>希望会后能跨工具持续推进工作、而不必在工具之间手动复制笔记的团队。</li> <li>需要在客户沟通、续约、实施或高管赞助人会议后跟进的客户团队。</li> <li>需要更新会议记录、文档、CRM 和团队消息的销售及客户成功工作流。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://marketplace.zoom.us/apps/w7dWfj-UQ5ihAmKdi3fykg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">zoom（需联网）</a></td> <td>在完成身份验证并获得管理员批准后，读取可访问的 Zoom 会议、录制内容、转录文本和 AI Companion 总结。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive（需联网）</a></td> <td>创建或起草客户账户计划、会议简报和其他可供审核的后续文档。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack（需联网）</a></td> <td>在你审核并批准团队消息后，起草团队更新。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>创建会后跟进材料包</p> <p>建议模型：<code>gpt-6-astra</code> · 建议推理级别：<code>low</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用我最近一次与 [customer or account] 有关的 Zoom 会议。\n\n获取该会议的转录文本和 AI Companion 总结。起草前，先指出你无法访问的内容。\n\n总结关键结论、决策、风险、机会和行动项。然后起草：\n- 一封发给客户的跟进邮件\n- 一份 Google Docs 客户账户计划\n- 一条 CRM 更新，包含笔记、风险、下一步和负责人\n- 一条发给 [team/channel/person] 的 Slack 消息，说明最重要的信息\n\n尽可能使用转录文本中的证据。标出不确定的内容，并确保客户邮件草稿不包含仅限内部的信息。\n\n在我逐项审核并批准之前，不要发送邮件、发布 Slack 消息、创建文档、更新 CRM 记录、指派负责人或泄露私人数据。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">计划任务</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"introduction\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">简介</h2> <p>客户沟通团队会花不少时间，在会议结束后把讨论内容转化为行动。一场会议可能产生跟进邮件、CRM 笔记、客户账户计划、风险更新和内部交接，但这些材料通常分散在不同系统里。</p> <p>连接 Zoom 和相关工具后，ChatGPT 可以读取相关转录文本和 AI Companion 总结，提取结构化信息，并准备后续工作所需的草稿。任何内容被发布、发送、指派或写入其他系统之前，你都可以先审核。</p> <p><a id=\"create-the-first-follow-up-package\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">创建第一份会后跟进材料包</h2> <ol> <li>启用 Zoom AI Companion 会议总结、智能录制、转录生成、云录制和音频转录。</li> <li>连接 Zoom 以及你希望 ChatGPT 使用的工具，例如 Google Docs、Slack、Gmail 或 CRM。</li> <li>按客户、日期、周期性会议系列或会议标题，请 ChatGPT 查找会议。</li> <li>审核生成的总结、风险、行动项、邮件草稿、客户账户计划、CRM 笔记和 Slack 消息。</li> <li>核对内容后，再批准任何会影响外部系统的操作。</li> </ol> <p>第一次使用时，可以采用本页的起始提示词。ChatGPT 应返回一份结构化材料包，包括关键结论、风险、机会、决策、行动项，以及跟进邮件草稿、客户账户计划大纲、CRM 更新草稿和 Slack 通知草稿。</p> <p><a id=\"give-chatgpt-the-right-context\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">提供合适的背景信息</h2> <p>要让这个工作流发挥作用，ChatGPT 需要读取会议来源材料，并了解每项后续内容应该放在哪里。</p> <p>有用的输入包括：</p> <ul> <li>Zoom 会议录制、转录文本和 AI Companion 总结。</li> <li>会议元数据，例如客户名称、日期、标题或周期性会议系列。</li> <li>目标工具，例如 Google Docs、Slack、Gmail 或 CRM 记录。</li> <li>语气、隐私、客户账户计划结构或内部交接格式方面的规则。</li> </ul> <p>之后，ChatGPT 可以总结转录文本、找出决策以及负责人和日期承诺、起草客户邮件、准备客户账户计划并撰写团队更新。对于周期性会议，它可以对照之前的通话，突出显示变化。</p> <p><a id=\"review-before-acting\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">执行前先审核</h2> <p>会后跟进可能涉及客户数据、私人笔记和权威记录系统。请先让 ChatGPT 准备草稿、引用转录文本中的证据，并暂存更新；只有你批准后再继续。</p> <p>采取行动前，请审核：</p> <ul> <li>接收对象或目标位置，例如客户、Slack 频道、CRM 记录，或文档权限。</li> <li>客户承诺、负责人、日期、风险和不确定说法。</li> <li>哪些内容应保留为草稿，哪些内容可以发送、发布、共享或保存。</li> <li>是否需要移除机密或仅限内部的信息。</li> </ul> <p>周期性工作流应保持简单：先起草，再审核、批准，最后执行。</p> <p><a id=\"follow-up-on-the-first-draft\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">根据第一份草稿继续跟进</h2> <p>第一份材料包准备好后，可以在同一聊天中继续调整，以适配不同读者或后续工作。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Make the follow-up email shorter and more executive-facing.\n\nKeep:\n\n- the customer commitment\n- the risks we need to acknowledge\n- the next meeting date\n\nRemove internal-only details. Do not send it yet.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">把这封后续跟进邮件改得更简短，并更适合管理层阅读。\n\n保留：\n\n- 对客户作出的承诺\n- 我们需要承认的风险\n- 下次会议日期\n\n删除仅供内部使用的细节。暂时不要发送。</div></div> <p>你也可以让 ChatGPT 将本次会议与前几周的会议进行比较、把行动项整理成双方行动计划、为销售工程师准备只包含技术阻碍的版本，或起草 CRM 更新但不保存。</p> <p><a id=\"automate-recurring-meeting-intelligence\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">自动化周期性会议情报整理</h2> <p>如果需要每周跟进客户或评审交易，可以固定该聊天，并请 ChatGPT <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations#schedule-a-task-inside-a-chat\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">为后续工作安排计划任务</a>（官网章节，需联网） <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">本地页面（本地尚未收录）</a>。</p> <p>你不一定希望 ChatGPT 自动发布内容，但它可以为你准备草稿；审核后，你再批准并发布。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Schedule a task from this chat to run after each weekly Zoom call with [customer]. Compare the new transcript and AI Companion summary against the prior three calls.\n\nDraft:\n\n- what changed\n- new risks or opportunities\n- action items with owners and dates\n- CRM notes\n- a Slack update for [team/channel]\n\nOnly update me when there is a meaningful change, a missing transcript, or a decision I need to make. Do not post, send, assign, or update external systems without approval.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">从这个聊天中安排一项任务，在每周与 [customer] 的 Zoom 通话结束后运行。将新的逐字稿和 AI Companion 摘要与此前三次通话进行比较。\n\n起草：\n\n- 发生了哪些变化\n- 新的风险或机会\n- 带有负责人和日期的行动项\n- CRM 记录\n- 发给 [team/channel] 的 Slack 更新\n\n只有出现实质性变化、缺少逐字稿，或有需要我作出的决定时，才向我更新。未经批准，不要发布、发送、指派任务或更新外部系统。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"turn-meetings-into-follow-ups\">Turn meetings into follow-ups</h1> <p>Convert Zoom meeting insights into actions across your tools.</p> <p>Use ChatGPT with Zoom transcripts and AI Companion summaries to draft customer follow-up emails, account plans, CRM updates, and team notifications for review.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Teams that want repeatable post-meeting execution without copying notes between tools.</li> <li>Customer follow-ups after discovery, renewal, implementation, or executive sponsor calls.</li> <li>Sales and customer success workflows that require updates across meeting notes, docs, CRM, and team messages.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://marketplace.zoom.us/apps/w7dWfj-UQ5ihAmKdi3fykg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">zoom (online)</a></td> <td>Read accessible Zoom meetings, recordings, transcripts, and AI Companion summaries after authentication and admin approval.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive (online)</a></td> <td>Create or draft account plans, meeting briefs, and other reviewable follow-up documents.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack (online)</a></td> <td>Draft team updates after the user reviews and approves the message.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Create a Post-Meeting Follow-Up Package</p> <p>Suggested model：<code>gpt-6-astra</code> · Suggested reasoning effort：<code>low</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use my most recent Zoom meeting with [customer or account].\n\nRetrieve the Zoom transcript and AI Companion summary. Name anything you cannot access before drafting.\n\nSummarize the key takeaways, decisions, risks, opportunities, and action items. Then draft:\n- a customer follow-up email\n- a Google Docs account plan\n- a CRM update with notes, risks, next steps, and owners\n- a Slack message to [team/channel/person] with the most important details\n\nUse evidence from the transcript where possible. Mark anything uncertain and keep internal-only details out of the customer draft.\n\nDo not send emails, post Slack messages, create docs, update CRM records, assign owners, or expose private data until I review and approve each action.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">Scheduled tasks</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"introduction\">Introduction</h2> <p>Customer-facing teams spend real time after meetings turning conversations into action. One call can create a follow-up email, CRM notes, an account plan, risk updates, and internal handoffs, but those artifacts usually live across separate systems.</p> <p>With Zoom meeting data and connected tools, ChatGPT can retrieve the relevant transcript and AI Companion summary, extract structured insights, and prepare the downstream drafts needed to move work forward. You stay in the review loop before anything is posted, sent, assigned, or written to another system.</p> <h2 id=\"create-the-first-follow-up-package\">Create the first follow-up package</h2> <ol> <li>Enable Zoom AI Companion meeting summaries, smart recordings, transcript generation, cloud recording, and audio transcripts.</li> <li>Connect Zoom and the tools you want ChatGPT to use, such as Google Docs, Slack, Gmail, or your CRM.</li> <li>Ask ChatGPT to find a meeting by customer, date, recurring series, or meeting title.</li> <li>Review the generated summary, risks, actions, email draft, account plan, CRM notes, and Slack message.</li> <li>Approve external actions only after validating the content.</li> </ol> <p>Use the starter prompt on this page for the first pass. ChatGPT should return a structured package with key takeaways, risks, opportunities, decisions, action items, a follow-up email draft, an account plan outline, a CRM update draft, and a Slack notification draft.</p> <h2 id=\"give-chatgpt-the-right-context\">Give ChatGPT the right context</h2> <p>This workflow works best when ChatGPT can read the meeting source material and knows where each follow-up should go.</p> <p>Useful inputs include:</p> <ul> <li>The Zoom meeting recording, transcript, and AI Companion summary.</li> <li>Meeting metadata such as customer name, date, title, or recurring series.</li> <li>The destination tools, such as Google Docs, Slack, Gmail, or CRM records.</li> <li>Any rules for tone, privacy, account-plan structure, or internal handoff format.</li> </ul> <p>ChatGPT can then summarize the transcript, identify decisions and owner/date commitments, draft a customer-facing email, prepare an account plan, and write a team update. For recurring meetings, it can compare the latest transcript against prior calls and highlight what changed.</p> <h2 id=\"review-before-acting\">Review before acting</h2> <p>Meeting follow-up can touch customer data, private notes, and systems of record. Use ChatGPT to prepare drafts, cite transcript evidence, and stage updates before you approve the next step.</p> <p>Before taking action, review:</p> <ul> <li>The audience or destination, such as the customer, Slack channel, CRM record, or document permissions.</li> <li>Customer commitments, owners, dates, risks, and uncertain claims.</li> <li>Which items should stay as drafts versus be sent, posted, shared, or saved.</li> <li>Whether confidential or internal-only details should be removed.</li> </ul> <p>For recurring workflows, keep the pattern focused: draft, review, approve, then act.</p> <h2 id=\"follow-up-on-the-first-draft\">Follow up on the first draft</h2> <p>After the first package is ready, use the same chat to tune it for the audience or next workflow.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Make the follow-up email shorter and more executive-facing.\n\nKeep:\n\n- the customer commitment\n- the risks we need to acknowledge\n- the next meeting date\n\nRemove internal-only details. Do not send it yet.\n</code></pre> <p>You can also ask ChatGPT to compare this call with the last few weekly calls, turn action items into a mutual action plan, create a version for a sales engineer with only technical blockers, or draft CRM updates without saving them.</p> <h2 id=\"automate-recurring-meeting-intelligence\">Automate recurring meeting intelligence</h2> <p>For weekly account check-ins or deal reviews, pin the chat and ask ChatGPT to <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations#schedule-a-task-inside-a-chat\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">schedule a task for the follow-up work from it</a> (official section, online) <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Local page (not in this local snapshot)</a>.</p> <p>You don't necessarily want ChatGPT to post automatically, but it can create drafts for your review that you can approve and post.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Schedule a task from this chat to run after each weekly Zoom call with [customer]. Compare the new transcript and AI Companion summary against the prior three calls.\n\nDraft:\n\n- what changed\n- new risks or opportunities\n- action items with owners and dates\n- CRM notes\n- a Slack update for [team/channel]\n\nOnly update me when there is a meaningful change, a missing transcript, or a decision I need to make. Do not post, send, assign, or update external systems without approval.\n</code></pre>"};
